# Explore — self-contained-renovacion-skill

## Area / focus
Whole repo exploration for converting `renovacion` into a self-contained Pi skill at `.pi/skills/renovacion/`, preserving `proyectos/[id]/` artifact convention and local testability.

## Current state
- Pi project skill discovery: Pi loads project skills from `.pi/skills/`; directories containing `SKILL.md` are discovered recursively. Skill `name` must match parent directory, lowercase letters/numbers/hyphens, <=64 chars, no leading/trailing/consecutive hyphens. `description` is required; missing description prevents load. Unknown frontmatter fields ignored. Skill instructions should reference scripts/assets via paths relative to skill directory.
- Repo has no `.pi/skills/` today. Existing Pi assets are agent prompts under `.pi/agents/renovacion-agent/` plus `.pi/agents/teams.yaml`; these are not skill packages.
- Existing artifact convention is consistent in docs and code: `proyectos/[id]/input.json`, `resultados.json`, `spec.json`, `memoria.html`, optional `memoria.pdf`, `assets/`.
- Golden project exists at `proyectos/1/` (`AURORA GMR`) with input/result/spec/memoria and staged assets.
- Engines:
  - `lib/input-pipeline/`: plain Python modules for validation/catalog/id. Depends on `jsonschema`; default paths resolve `rules/renovacion.json` and `proyectos/` from three parents above module, which will work if copied under skill root as `lib/input-pipeline/`.
  - `lib/calc-engine/`: Python package under `src/calc_engine`; `run_calculation(input_path, rules_path, output_path)` works. Tests pass only when run from `lib/calc-engine` via `uv run`.
  - `lib/spec-engine/`: Python modules in hyphenated directory. `runner.py` uses relative imports, but directory name is not importable as `spec_engine` without a wrapper/alias or layout change. Custom `tests/spec-engine/run_tests.py` loads modules by path, but pytest imports fail.
  - `lib/memory-engine/`: Node CommonJS, no npm runtime deps. Uses `__dirname` for CSS (`../../assets/css`) but uses `process.cwd()`/`path.resolve()` for default project path and catalog image resolution. Works when executed from repo/skill root.
- Existing commands:
  - `bash scripts/run-project-1.sh` passes from repo root; it checks existing calc/spec artifacts, runs memory engine, validates no CDN and expected content.
  - `cd lib/calc-engine && uv run pytest ../../tests/calc-engine -q` passes: 35 tests.
  - `uv run --with jsonschema pytest -q tests/input-pipeline` mostly works but has 2 failing dimension-note assertions.
  - `python tests/spec-engine/run_tests.py` passes 11 custom tests; pytest collection for spec fails due import/package layout and duplicate `test_runner.py` module names.
  - Memory smoke/regression plain node test `tests/memory-engine/regression-hardening.test.js` passes, but most memory tests use Jest globals without package/runner and fail under plain `node`. `tests/memory-engine/integration.test.js` is stale: expects `cdn.jsdelivr.net`, contradicting current vendored KaTeX implementation.

