## Technical findings
- Pi skill requirement: `SKILL.md` frontmatter must include `name: renovacion` and `description`; `name` must match `.pi/skills/renovacion` parent. Missing description = not loaded. Pi is lenient on many validation issues but warns.
- Pi loads project `.pi/skills/` from cwd and ancestors up to repo root; local testing can run from repo root or inside skill dir. Skill content should use relative paths from skill dir.
- Existing `run-project-1.sh` already computes `REPO_ROOT` from script location, so copied script naturally treats `.pi/skills/renovacion` as root. Good base.
- `memory-engine/runner.js` defaults `projectPath` from `process.cwd()`. If invoked from outside skill root, it may read/write wrong `proyectos/`. Wrapper should `cd` skill root or pass explicit project path.
- `memory-engine/assets.js` resolves catalog image refs with `path.resolve(imageRef)`, also cwd-sensitive. Wrapper `cd` skill root is safest minimal fix.
- `memory-engine/formula.js` emits KaTeX paths as `../../assets/vendor/katex/...`, valid only when `memoria.html` lives under `proyectos/[id]/` under same root as `assets/`. Preserves current convention; not project-folder-portable by itself.
- Input pipeline default `rules` and `proyectos` paths should work after copying because `Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent` from `lib/input-pipeline` points to skill root.
- Calc engine has no standalone CLI except `scripts/generate_golden_example.py`; existing smoke does not recompute `resultados.json`.
- Spec engine has no CLI that writes `spec.json`; README shows manual Python code. Need wrapper for end-to-end skill use.
- Current root `pyproject.toml` has no `jsonschema`, so input-pipeline tests fail unless using `uv run --with jsonschema` or adding dependency. Skill-local pyproject should fix this.
- No `package.json`; runtime Node code is stdlib-only. Jest-style tests cannot run without adding a test dependency or rewriting to plain node.

