## Risks / pitfalls
- Copying files without wrappers may appear self-contained but write/read root `proyectos/` when scripts are invoked from repo root or Pi session cwd outside skill dir.
- Spec engine hyphenated folder is biggest Python import pitfall for wrappers/tests.
- `jsonschema` missing from root deps will make skill tests flaky unless skill-local dependency handling is explicit.
- Existing smoke is not full end-to-end; it relies on committed `resultados.json` and `spec.json`. Planner should decide whether smoke means baseline render or true recompute.
- Catalog references missing images (`ex-100`, inyectores) while assets only include selected extractor images. Either include all referenced assets, prune/update catalog, or accept placeholder warnings.
- Memory HTML references shared `../../assets/vendor/katex`, not project-local `proyectos/[id]/assets/vendor`; OK for skill-contained tree, not OK if only project folder copied.
- Logo URLs in `input.json` can trigger network downloads; current committed project assets make smoke fast, but regenerating from clean project may depend on network unless placeholders/asset seeding are used.
- Existing `.pi/agents` prompts mention optional PDF; approved skill scope says do not finalize install instructions, and current engine does not produce PDF. SKILL.md should avoid promising PDF generation.

## Recommendation for planning
- Treat `.pi/skills/renovacion/` as a copied mini-root with its own `proyectos/`, `lib/`, `rules/`, `assets/`, `docs/contracts/`, `scripts/`, fixtures, and test metadata.
- Add path-stable wrappers that compute `SKILL_ROOT` from script location and `cd` there before calling Python/Node. Preserve `proyectos/[id]/` relative to skill root.
- Add a skill-structure test first: frontmatter valid, `name` matches parent, required files exist, KaTeX/assets/rules/catalog present.
- Add a smoke test that runs from `.pi/skills/renovacion/` and proves no root files are needed. Prefer a true e2e wrapper if budget allows; otherwise clearly name current smoke as baseline-memory smoke.
- Use plain Python/Node/bash tests for skill validation; avoid introducing Jest unless needed.
- Do not update README install instructions in this change; keep usage/test notes inside `SKILL.md` or skill-local docs only.

